# Bookstore

Generated by pangolin 0.1.0. Go 1.27.4, Docker Compose and an available loopback port are required. Run commands from this project directory.

```powershell
go mod tidy
go test ./...
docker compose up -d --build
curl.exe http://localhost:18281/readyz
$token = (Invoke-RestMethod -Method Post http://localhost:18280/token -ContentType application/json -Body '{"subject":"alice","tenant_id":"tenant-a"}').access_token
$headers = @{Authorization="Bearer $token";'Idempotency-Key'='first-book'}
Invoke-RestMethod -Method Post http://localhost:18281/books -Headers $headers -ContentType application/json -Body '{"id":"book-1","title":"Go in Practice"}'
Invoke-RestMethod http://localhost:18281/books/book-1 -Headers $headers
```

Expected: readiness returns 204, POST and GET return the same book. Repeating the same key/body replays the result; another body with that key conflicts. Tokens and seeded memberships belong to this disposable local fixture. The unauthenticated IdP and public local passwords must be replaced for deployment.

The bundled `framework/` is the exact version-bound runtime source, with checksums in runtime-manifest.json. Its local module replacement permits pre-release use before the version is published. Keep the bundle and generator version together. After publication an application may replace the bundle with the equivalent tagged dependency, following its own upgrade review.

Business layers live in internal/domain, internal/application and internal/infrastructure. Application depends on Ports. HTTP uses JWT verification, current Tenant authority, exact Scope binding, explicit Permission, strict decoding and a short UOW. Reads use read-only transactions. Writes atomically save the book, required Audit, versioned Outbox fact and idempotency result; 2xx is sent after confirmed Commit. Outbox rows are durable; a delivery Worker/Broker is a separate deployment concern. The generated API does not promise external delivery without that Worker.

Run `pangolin module add catalog --depends persistence,authorization`, then `pangolin migrate create add_books --module catalog`. The module joins the explicit registry; edit its Module() to register real providers. Fill the generated Goose migration before applying it with `PANGOLIN_MIGRATION_DSN` and `go run ./cmd/migrate`. Only the deployment command applies migrations; API startup checks compatibility. `pangolin migrate status` reads the Goose ledger. `pangolin doctor` checks project/runtime/tooling; `pangolin generate openapi` writes the profile's OpenAPI 3.1 document while preserving a modified file.

Server shutdown first stops admission and drains active operations, then closes owned pools. Missing membership, unsupported scope and permission failures fail closed. Unknown Commit results retain their operation identity; retry using the original idempotency key. Cache/Settings/Features are available in the bundled runtime and can be injected explicitly.

Use `PANGOLIN_PG_PORT`, `PANGOLIN_IDP_PORT`, `PANGOLIN_API_PORT` to isolate multiple Compose projects. Cleanup your own environment with `docker compose down --volumes --rmi local`. See PROFILE.md for profile-specific routes and boundaries. Tests with real services are run by the framework's generated-template acceptance runner; plain go test tests the generated domain without external services.
